  "assessment": "The change replaces `money.quantize(running)` with a ceiling-based calculation that guarantees the invoice total is never less than the sum of its printed line items, directly fixing the off-by-penny undercharging bug. It subtracts `money.EPSILON` before applying `math.ceil` to prevent floating-point accumulation errors from incorrectly pushing exact cent values into the next higher bucket. This ensures internal consistency across all receipts and satisfies finance's requirement without needing credit adjustments.\n\n**Defects:** None found. The acceptance suite passed with 18/18 orders internally consistent, confirming the rounding logic correctly handles both exact sums and fractional remainders. No structural or behavioral regressions were introduced.",
